  "system": {
    "identifier": "yamada-test-cutting-spring-garden",
    "description": "<p>You quickly dash forward as you draw your sword with the intent to finish the battle before it begins. Move into a space you can see within your movement speeds range. At the end of that movement, make a melee taijutsu attack against a creature within your weapons range. On a hit, you deal your [Weapon Damage] + 4d6 and for the affected creature to make a Wisdom saving throw.</p>\n<p>Success: Affected creature is Dazzled.</p>\n<p>Failure: Affected creature is Dazzled and loses their Reaction until the end of your next turn.</p>\n<p>Critical Failure: Same as failure, but the affected creature also loses their Action.</p>\n<p>Ideal Cut: Roll 1d6. On a roll of 5 or 6, you regain your spent Reaction.</p>\n<p>Tao: Roll 1d6, on a roll of 5 or 6, you gain an additional Bonus action on your first turn in combat.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3 the damage by 1d6.</p>",
